# Binaries and test outputs
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
/alloca-go
/bin/
/dist/
/coverage/
coverage.out

# Delve debug binaries (e.g. cmd/alloca-go/__debug_bin*)
__debug_bin*

# Go workspace and local tooling
go.work
go.work.sum

# Local environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.local

# Claude Code's project directory, ignored whole. `settings.local.json` is personal and
# already excluded globally; `settings.json` is nominally the shareable file, but its
# entries accrete from whichever permission prompts were approved in a session, so it
# lands in a commit by accident rather than by decision — which is how it reached this
# branch in the first place.
#
# The directory can also hold hand-authored tooling (slash commands, subagents, skills,
# hook scripts). Nancy's call, 2026-08-06: none of it belongs in this repo for now, so
# the whole directory is ignored rather than the settings files named individually. If
# that changes, `git add -f` the specific file — and note the ignore means a new one
# will not show up in `git status` to remind you.
/.claude/

# IDE and editor files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Operating-system files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs and generated benchmark data
*.log
/tmp/

# Local load-harness output. A run worth keeping is promoted into
# docs/measurements/ deliberately; everything else is scratch, and leaving it in
# the repo root is how it ends up committed by accident.
/test/results/

# Terraform local state and plans
**/.terraform/*
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

# Local secrets
*.pem
*.key

# Discovered Prometheus scrape targets: a property of the machine, not the project.
/deploy/observability/targets/*.json
